encyclopedia :auneth do
  name "Auneth"
  summary "Auneth are large armored grazers of Korvath's sheltered seabeds, carrying small communities across the coast on overlapping porous plates."
  kind :lifeform
  subkind :animal
  status :complete
  topics :ecology, :materials, :subject_planetary_life
  prevalence :rare
  appears_when all: { place: [:outer_system, :waterway] }
  biology "A broad bottom-grazer propelled by rows of muscular feet beneath a layered mineral-and-fiber carapace"
  principal_accommodation "Warm shallow coastal water with extensive grazing surfaces and room to turn"
  descriptive_identity appearance: "A low oval carapace rises like a broken terrace above hundreds of slow pale feet; small animals occupy grooves between its plates.", behavior: "An auneth grazes steadily along familiar seabed contours and folds its feet under the shell when disturbed.", threat: "A turning adult can crush a small boat against stone or block the only deep entrance to a pool."
  prose <<~PROSE
    Auneth move across warm seabeds on rows of short muscular feet. Their overlapping plates carry grooves and sheltered pores where small animals settle. An old adult can bear a patchwork of colored growth large enough to mistake for part of the shore. The mouth lies beneath the forward edge, grazing films and soft encrusting life from the ground while the upper community travels undisturbed.

    Along the quieter reaches beyond #{ref :oskara}, fishers recognize individuals by broken plate margins and the growth they carry. A storm can drive a young auneth into an enclosed pool it entered easily and cannot leave at the next low tide. At #{ref :kethra}, residents measure the inner pool's grazing surface before agreeing to receive one. A refuge that keeps the animal safe from hunters may still starve it.

    The #{ref :ilvaren, "Ilvaren"} publish drawings of naturally loosening plate edges so collectors can gather #{encyclopedia_ref :auneth_lamina} without cutting living armor. Dealers pay more for broad clean sheets than for irregular shed pieces. Some employ keepers to wait through a shedding; others pry plates loose and leave wounds among the remaining layers. An injured animal may fold down over its feet, becoming almost impossible to move without clearing the water around it.
  PROSE
  cue "A patch of apparently fixed reef begins crossing the pale bottom, carrying its small fish with it."
  cue "Hundreds of feet disappear beneath the armored rim, leaving the pool's entrance blocked by a motionless oval."
  affordance "Recognizing a loosening outer plate allows a collector to recover valuable lamina without opening a wound."
  pressure "A sheltered pool can protect an auneth while providing too little grazing ground to sustain it."
  variation "Young animals carry relatively smooth armor and can pass through channels too narrow for an adult."
  variation "Old adults support elaborate living growth and shed irregular plates valuable to collectors despite their damaged edges."
  log "2026-09-20 — Galaxy's Child supplied care for a large animal whose needs conflict with a vessel's occupants; the result is a coastal grazer with finite refuge space, not a ship-feeding space creature: https://www.startrek.com/news/no-negotiation."
end
